{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Hotkeys provides the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeySequenceRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" composable for building UIs where users record multi-chord sequences (Vim-style shortcuts). The recorder captures each step like a single hotkey chord. Users finish with Enter by default, or you can use manual commit and an optional idle timeout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequence recording uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordBy: 'code'"},{"type":"text","value":" by default, preserving every step as a physical string such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['[KeyG]', 'Alt+[KeyS]']"},{"type":"text","value":". Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordBy: 'key'"},{"type":"text","value":" for logical characters. The shared rejection and conflict options follow the "},{"type":"link","href":"./hotkey-recording.md#validation-and-conflicts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkey recording guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"},{"type":"text","value":". Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reactive-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recorder options support "},{"type":"link","href":"./hotkeys.md#property-getters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"property getters and functions returning options"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Updated callbacks, validation, and recording settings apply during an active session without restarting it. Allow the framework to run its effect or watcher before relying on the update."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { formatForDisplay, useHotkeySequenceRecorder } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\nimport type { HotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst { isRecording, recordedSequence, startRecording, cancelRecording } =\n  useHotkeySequenceRecorder({\n    onRecord: (sequence: HotkeySequence) => {\n      console.log('Recorded:', sequence)\n    },\n  })\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      @click=\"isRecording ? cancelRecording() : startRecording()\"\n    >\n      {{\n        isRecording\n          ? 'Press chords, then Enter...'\n          : recordedSequence\n            ? recordedSequence.map((h) => formatForDisplay(h)).join(' ')\n            : 'Click to record'\n      }}\n    </button>\n    <button v-if=\"isRecording\" type=\"button\" @click=\"cancelRecording()\">\n      Cancel\n    </button>\n  </div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"return-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return value"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether the recorder is listening"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"steps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chords captured in the current session"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordedSequence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Last committed sequence"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start a new session"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stopRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop without calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop and call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commit current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"steps"},{"type":"text","value":" (no-op if empty)"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordBy"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'code'"},{"type":"text","value":"; choose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'key'"},{"type":"text","value":" for logical characters. Repeats and IME composition never append steps. Modifier-only presses wait for a complete chord."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core options live on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequenceRecorderOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/hotkeys"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord(sequence)"},{"type":"text","value":": called when a nonempty sequence is committed. Clearing calls only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":": same intent as the hotkey recorder."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitKeys"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'enter'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default) or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'none'"},{"type":"text","value":". With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'none'"},{"type":"text","value":", only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitRecording()"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idleTimeoutMs"},{"type":"text","value":") finishes recording; plain Enter can be recorded as a chord."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitOnEnter"},{"type":"text","value":": when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitKeys"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'enter'"},{"type":"text","value":", set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to treat Enter as a normal chord (then use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitRecording()"},{"type":"text","value":" or idle timeout to finish)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idleTimeoutMs"},{"type":"text","value":": optional milliseconds of inactivity after the last completed chord to auto-commit. The timer does not run while waiting for the first chord."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"provider-defaults","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider defaults"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<HotkeysProvider\n  defaultOptions={{\n    hotkeySequenceRecorder: {\n      idleTimeoutMs: 2000,\n    },\n  }}\n>\n  <App />\n</HotkeysProvider>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ignoreinputs","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ignoreInputs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequenceRecorderOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" supports an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ignoreInputs"},{"type":"text","value":" option (defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":"). When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the recorder doesn't intercept normal typing in text inputs, textareas, selects, or contentEditable elements; keystrokes pass through to the input as usual. Pressing Escape still cancels recording even when an input has focus. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ignoreInputs: false"},{"type":"text","value":" if you want the recorder to capture keys from within input elements."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validation-and-conflicts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation and conflicts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequence "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validate(sequence, { events, parsedSequence })"},{"type":"text","value":" runs when committing and returns true, false, or a rejection message. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detectConflicts"},{"type":"text","value":" checks sequence prefixes as well as single bindings. Rejected commits keep recording active with the steps intact so the user can edit them with Backspace. Empty Backspace/Delete clears and emits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":" only; removing a nonempty step does not commit. Recorded steps, commit keys, and releases are isolated from application handlers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Valid chord"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Appended to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"steps"},{"type":"text","value":"; listener stays active"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enter (no modifiers), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitKeys: 'enter'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"steps.length >= 1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commits and calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Escape"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancels; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Backspace / Delete (no modifiers)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removes last step, or if empty runs only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":" and stops"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recorded chords use portable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod"},{"type":"text","value":" format, same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"under-the-hood","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeySequenceRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" wraps the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequenceRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" class and subscribes to its TanStack Store, same pattern as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"reactive-options","text":"Reactive options","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic usage","level":2},{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"provider-defaults","text":"Provider defaults","level":3},{"id":"ignoreinputs","text":"ignoreInputs","level":3},{"id":"validation-and-conflicts","text":"Validation and conflicts","level":2},{"id":"behavior","text":"Behavior","level":2},{"id":"under-the-hood","text":"Under the hood","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Hotkeys provides the `useHotkeySequenceRecorder` composable for building UIs where users record multi-chord sequences (Vim-style shortcuts). The recorder captures each step like a single hotkey chord. Users finish with Enter by default, or you can use manual commit and an optional idle timeout.\n\nSequence recording uses `recordBy: 'code'` by default, preserving every step as a physical string such as `['[KeyG]', 'Alt+[KeyS]']`. Set `recordBy: 'key'` for logical characters. The shared rejection and conflict options follow the [hotkey recording guide](./hotkey-recording.md#validation-and-conflicts).\n\nTanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set `enabled` from `isRecording`. Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release.\n\n## Reactive options\n\nRecorder options support [property getters and functions returning options](./hotkeys.md#property-getters). Updated callbacks, validation, and recording settings apply during an active session without restarting it. Allow the framework to run its effect or watcher before relying on the update.\n\n## Basic usage\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { formatForDisplay, useHotkeySequenceRecorder } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\nimport type { HotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst { isRecording, recordedSequence, startRecording, cancelRecording } =\n  useHotkeySequenceRecorder({\n    onRecord: (sequence: HotkeySequence) => {\n      console.log('Recorded:', sequence)\n    },\n  })\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      @click=\"isRecording ? cancelRecording() : startRecording()\"\n    >\n      {{\n        isRecording\n          ? 'Press chords, then Enter...'\n          : recordedSequence\n            ? recordedSequence.map((h) => formatForDisplay(h)).join(' ')\n            : 'Click to record'\n      }}\n    </button>\n    <button v-if=\"isRecording\" type=\"button\" @click=\"cancelRecording()\">\n      Cancel\n    </button>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\n## Return value\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `isRecording` | `boolean` | Whether the recorder is listening |\n| `steps` | `HotkeySequence` | Chords captured in the current session |\n| `recordedSequence` | `HotkeySequence \\| null` | Last committed sequence |\n| `startRecording` | `() => void` | Start a new session |\n| `stopRecording` | `() => void` | Stop without calling `onRecord` |\n| `cancelRecording` | `() => void` | Stop and call `onCancel` |\n| `commitRecording` | `() => void` | Commit current `steps` (no-op if empty) |\n\n## Options\n\n`recordBy` defaults to `'code'`; choose `'key'` for logical characters. Repeats and IME composition never append steps. Modifier-only presses wait for a complete chord.\n\nCore options live on `HotkeySequenceRecorderOptions` from `@tanstack/hotkeys`:\n\n- `onRecord(sequence)`: called when a nonempty sequence is committed. Clearing calls only `onClear`.\n- `onCancel`, `onClear`: same intent as the hotkey recorder.\n- `commitKeys`: `'enter'` (default) or `'none'`. With `'none'`, only `commitRecording()` (or `idleTimeoutMs`) finishes recording; plain Enter can be recorded as a chord.\n- `commitOnEnter`: when `commitKeys` is `'enter'`, set to `false` to treat Enter as a normal chord (then use `commitRecording()` or idle timeout to finish).\n- `idleTimeoutMs`: optional milliseconds of inactivity after the last completed chord to auto-commit. The timer does not run while waiting for the first chord.\n\n### Provider defaults\n\n```vue\n<HotkeysProvider\n  defaultOptions={{\n    hotkeySequenceRecorder: {\n      idleTimeoutMs: 2000,\n    },\n  }}\n>\n  <App />\n</HotkeysProvider>\n```\n\n### `ignoreInputs`\n\nThe `HotkeySequenceRecorderOptions` supports an `ignoreInputs` option (defaults to `true`). When `true`, the recorder doesn't intercept normal typing in text inputs, textareas, selects, or contentEditable elements; keystrokes pass through to the input as usual. Pressing Escape still cancels recording even when an input has focus. Set `ignoreInputs: false` if you want the recorder to capture keys from within input elements.\n\n## Validation and conflicts\n\nSequence `validate(sequence, { events, parsedSequence })` runs when committing and returns true, false, or a rejection message. `detectConflicts` checks sequence prefixes as well as single bindings. Rejected commits keep recording active with the steps intact so the user can edit them with Backspace. Empty Backspace/Delete clears and emits `onClear` only; removing a nonempty step does not commit. Recorded steps, commit keys, and releases are isolated from application handlers.\n\n## Behavior\n\n| Input | Behavior |\n|-------|----------|\n| Valid chord | Appended to `steps`; listener stays active |\n| Enter (no modifiers), `commitKeys: 'enter'`, `steps.length >= 1` | Commits and calls `onRecord` |\n| Escape | Cancels; `onCancel` |\n| Backspace / Delete (no modifiers) | Removes last step, or if empty runs only `onClear` and stops |\n\nRecorded chords use portable `Mod` format, same as `HotkeyRecorder`.\n\n## Under the hood\n\n`useHotkeySequenceRecorder` wraps the `HotkeySequenceRecorder` class and subscribes to its TanStack Store, same pattern as `useHotkeyRecorder`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Sequence Recording Guide\nid: sequence-recording\n---\n\nTanStack Hotkeys provides the `useHotkeySequenceRecorder` composable for building UIs where users record multi-chord sequences (Vim-style shortcuts). The recorder captures each step like a single hotkey chord. Users finish with Enter by default, or you can use manual commit and an optional idle timeout.\n\nSequence recording uses `recordBy: 'code'` by default, preserving every step as a physical string such as `['[KeyG]', 'Alt+[KeyS]']`. Set `recordBy: 'key'` for logical characters. The shared rejection and conflict options follow the [hotkey recording guide](./hotkey-recording.md#validation-and-conflicts).\n\nTanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set `enabled` from `isRecording`. Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release.\n\n## Reactive options\n\nRecorder options support [property getters and functions returning options](./hotkeys.md#property-getters). Updated callbacks, validation, and recording settings apply during an active session without restarting it. Allow the framework to run its effect or watcher before relying on the update.\n\n## Basic usage\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { formatForDisplay, useHotkeySequenceRecorder } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\nimport type { HotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst { isRecording, recordedSequence, startRecording, cancelRecording } =\n  useHotkeySequenceRecorder({\n    onRecord: (sequence: HotkeySequence) => {\n      console.log('Recorded:', sequence)\n    },\n  })\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      @click=\"isRecording ? cancelRecording() : startRecording()\"\n    >\n      {{\n        isRecording\n          ? 'Press chords, then Enter...'\n          : recordedSequence\n            ? recordedSequence.map((h) => formatForDisplay(h)).join(' ')\n            : 'Click to record'\n      }}\n    </button>\n    <button v-if=\"isRecording\" type=\"button\" @click=\"cancelRecording()\">\n      Cancel\n    </button>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\n## Return value\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `isRecording` | `boolean` | Whether the recorder is listening |\n| `steps` | `HotkeySequence` | Chords captured in the current session |\n| `recordedSequence` | `HotkeySequence \\| null` | Last committed sequence |\n| `startRecording` | `() => void` | Start a new session |\n| `stopRecording` | `() => void` | Stop without calling `onRecord` |\n| `cancelRecording` | `() => void` | Stop and call `onCancel` |\n| `commitRecording` | `() => void` | Commit current `steps` (no-op if empty) |\n\n## Options\n\n`recordBy` defaults to `'code'`; choose `'key'` for logical characters. Repeats and IME composition never append steps. Modifier-only presses wait for a complete chord.\n\nCore options live on `HotkeySequenceRecorderOptions` from `@tanstack/hotkeys`:\n\n- `onRecord(sequence)`: called when a nonempty sequence is committed. Clearing calls only `onClear`.\n- `onCancel`, `onClear`: same intent as the hotkey recorder.\n- `commitKeys`: `'enter'` (default) or `'none'`. With `'none'`, only `commitRecording()` (or `idleTimeoutMs`) finishes recording; plain Enter can be recorded as a chord.\n- `commitOnEnter`: when `commitKeys` is `'enter'`, set to `false` to treat Enter as a normal chord (then use `commitRecording()` or idle timeout to finish).\n- `idleTimeoutMs`: optional milliseconds of inactivity after the last completed chord to auto-commit. The timer does not run while waiting for the first chord.\n\n### Provider defaults\n\n```vue\n<HotkeysProvider\n  defaultOptions={{\n    hotkeySequenceRecorder: {\n      idleTimeoutMs: 2000,\n    },\n  }}\n>\n  <App />\n</HotkeysProvider>\n```\n\n### `ignoreInputs`\n\nThe `HotkeySequenceRecorderOptions` supports an `ignoreInputs` option (defaults to `true`). When `true`, the recorder doesn't intercept normal typing in text inputs, textareas, selects, or contentEditable elements; keystrokes pass through to the input as usual. Pressing Escape still cancels recording even when an input has focus. Set `ignoreInputs: false` if you want the recorder to capture keys from within input elements.\n\n## Validation and conflicts\n\nSequence `validate(sequence, { events, parsedSequence })` runs when committing and returns true, false, or a rejection message. `detectConflicts` checks sequence prefixes as well as single bindings. Rejected commits keep recording active with the steps intact so the user can edit them with Backspace. Empty Backspace/Delete clears and emits `onClear` only; removing a nonempty step does not commit. Recorded steps, commit keys, and releases are isolated from application handlers.\n\n## Behavior\n\n| Input | Behavior |\n|-------|----------|\n| Valid chord | Appended to `steps`; listener stays active |\n| Enter (no modifiers), `commitKeys: 'enter'`, `steps.length >= 1` | Commits and calls `onRecord` |\n| Escape | Cancels; `onCancel` |\n| Backspace / Delete (no modifiers) | Removes last step, or if empty runs only `onClear` and stops |\n\nRecorded chords use portable `Mod` format, same as `HotkeyRecorder`.\n\n## Under the hood\n\n`useHotkeySequenceRecorder` wraps the `HotkeySequenceRecorder` class and subscribes to its TanStack Store, same pattern as `useHotkeyRecorder`.\n"}
